 reasoning_trace="""Name and version intent: "Affiliate Management v1" — affiliates who sell, fraud that does not pay. Preconditions: tracking platform live; terms drafted; payout process finance-approved. Steps: Step 1 (Manager): affiliate vetting — traffic source declared, audience fit checked (wikipedia-marketing-clusters#30: bad affiliates exploit commission claims); artifact: vetting log; verification: no approval without declared source. Step 2 (Ops): enablement — unique links, swipe copy, creative; artifact: affiliate kit; verification: kit issued per affiliate. Step 3 (Analyst): monthly fraud review — self-referrals, cookie stuffing patterns, brand-term bidding violations; artifact: fraud report; verification: every payout cross-checked. Approval gates: Tier 1 — affiliate approved to join; Tier 2 — payouts human-approved monthly. Zero custody: the agent never holds commission funds or payment credentials — payouts execute through finance; the agent's job is the fraud report, not the money. Failure modes: fraud detected (clawback per terms, ban); brand bidding violation (warn once, then ban). Attribution note: affiliate revenue vs. cost; honest note that incrementality varies.""",
