 brief={'objective':'Generate the SEO reporting playbook.','audience':'SEO teams reporting to executives.','constraints':'Must kill vanity reporting.'},
 reasoning_trace="""Name and version intent: "SEO Reporting v1" — reports that drive decisions. Preconditions: rank tracking; analytics with revenue attribution; competitor set defined. Steps: Step 1 (Analyst): rankings by intent segment (not just head terms); artifact: segment table; verification: brand vs. non-brand split explicit. Step 2 (Analyst): organic traffic by page type + share of voice vs. competitors; artifact: trend charts; verification: trends, not snapshots. Step 3 (Analyst): revenue/assisted revenue from organic; artifact: revenue table; verification: attribution method footnoted. Never "total organic traffic" alone — it mixes brand and non-brand into a meaningless number (1s-ahrefs-blog#6). Every chart labels what is measured vs. modeled — modeled numbers wear the 'modeled' label, never presented as measured; the report offers no invented attribution, the method is footnoted and the uncertainty stated. Approval gates: Tier 1 — report template approved quarterly. Failure modes: data breaks (flag, do not interpolate silently); stakeholder asks for vanity metrics (include as appendix, never headline). Attribution note: the report carries its own attribution note — SEO investments pay out over four quarters; judge on trends and cohorts, not weeks.""",
