 reasoning_trace="""Name and version intent: "Search-Term Mining v1" — turns query data into profit. Preconditions: conversion tracking live; search-term reports accessible; negative list exists. Steps: Step 1 (Analyst): pull the search-term report weekly; artifact: raw report; verification: full week, all campaigns. Step 2 (Analyst): harvest — queries that convert become exact-match keywords; artifact: harvest list; verification: each harvest has ≥2 conversions. Step 3 (Analyst): add negatives — irrelevant themes (jobs, free, DIY) blocked; artifact: negative list update; verification: negatives applied, spend on junk queries tracked to zero (1s-google-skillshop#2: a neglected negative list is the #1 source of wasted spend; 1s-amazon-ads-learning#7: the weekly harvest/negate loop). Approval gates: Tier 1 — weekly mining reviewed (15 min); Tier 2 — budget shifts from findings. Autopilot never buys media — findings become proposals; every budget shift stops at human approval. Failure modes: report ignored for 3 weeks (escalate — the habit is the playbook); negatives over-applied (audit quarterly for blocked winners). Attribution note: wasted-spend trend and harvested-winner performance; honest note that attribution windows lag.""",
