 brief={'objective':'Generate the webinar production playbook.','audience':'Demand gen teams running monthly webinars.','constraints':'Must protect the follow-up, not just the live event.'},
 reasoning_trace="""Name and version intent: "Webinar Production v1" — the webinar is the middle; the follow-up is the payoff. Preconditions: topic with a named takeaway; speaker confirmed; registration page + CRM sync live. Steps: Step 1 (Producer): the promise — one sentence, one takeaway, named in the title (vague topics produce vague registrations); artifact: title + takeaway doc; verification: 5 strangers can state the takeaway. Step 2 (Ops): tech rehearsal — slides, polls, the handoff to sales defined by behavior (attended + engaged); artifact: rehearsal checklist signed; verification: dry run completed 48h before. Step 3 (Demand): promotion — 3 emails to the house list, partner sends if co-marketing; artifact: send log; verification: sends confirmed. Step 4 (Producer): live execution — polls every 15 min, Q&A harvested for content; artifact: recording + Q&A export; verification: recording processed in 24h. Step 5 (Ops): the follow-up — attendees vs. no-shows tracks, sales handoff by behavior; artifact: follow-up completion log; verification: every registrant touched in 72h (1s-hubspot-academy#5: the follow-up is where webinars pay). Approval gates: Tier 1 — topic + takeaway; Tier 1 — slide deck; Tier 2 — the offer made on the webinar. Failure modes: low registration (sharpen the promise, not the ad spend); tech failure mid-live (backup line, recording-first fallback). Attribution note: pipeline per webinar vs. the program's cost; honest note that multi-touch confounds.""",
